    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#constantinople">Constantinople</a>, whose people called themselves Romans for over 1,100 years.</li><li>It preserved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#roman-law">Roman law</a> in Justinian's Code and Greek learning, and spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Christianity</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#balkans">Balkans</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a> in 1071 and the crusader sack of 1204 crippled it; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1453.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>, completed under Justinian in 537, remained the largest church in the world for nearly a thousand years.</p></aside>
    </section>

